# Milestone: M3
# Covers: onleave handler runs when the tagged block exits normally
#         (no stop/throw); side-effect variable is set by the onleave body.
#
# defer-to: T29
#
# Reason: the `onleave` keyword and its parse + emit path are not yet wired at
# M3.  The TAG_SCOPE cleanup-entry FLAG_HAS_ONLEAVE flag and
# run_cleanup_with_replace() plumbing are already in place (T11), but the
# lexer/parser does not yet recognise the `onleave` keyword and the emit path
# does not generate FLAG_HAS_ONLEAVE entries.  The keyword is likely not
# introduced until M5 reactive runtime.  Defer to T29 or the M5 reactive
# milestone — whichever lands `onleave` parse/emit first.
#
# When onleave parse/emit is available, implement this fixture by uncommenting
# the source below.  Expected behaviour: onleave body sets side=99 on normal
# block exit.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29 / M5):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var side = 0;
#   t: { side = 1 } onleave { side = 99 };
#   side
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 99
